(2792032, 386739, 56254, '<td valign="top">too bad the sky wasn''t more interesting when you took this picture ... the green is great though ...<br/> <br/>edit, two days later ... after reviewing this photo again, I''d like to retract my previous comment ... I think the lack of interest in the sky really helps this image ... I''m bumping from a 7 to an 8 ...</td>', 'too bad the sky wasn''t more interesting when you took this picture ... the green is great though ... edit, two days later ... after reviewing this photo again, I''d like to retract my previous comment ... I think the lack of interest in the sky really helps this image ... I''m bumping from a 7 to an 8 ...', '2006-09-03 14:21:21.000000', NULL, 1),
(2792033, 386827, 50034, '<td valign="top"><b>Cute!  I get the humor.</b>  If only it was not such a serious subject in the original meaning.   <br/> <i>When I was still <b>a sophomoric teenager</b> (of course, my friends would all say, <b>"Sorry, Dude, mentally No Change today"</b>,) I tried to create my own humor by teasing that the untimely deaths of "Snap, Crackle &amp; Pop" would be performed by a "cereal" killer.  Very Dark Humor...</i>  :(<br/>       But as to meeting the challenge,...<b>Dead On!</b>   I give you a 9 for challenge parameters.  I would give you a 10, but IMHO the contrast was post-processed too thin.  Nothing more than a judgment call on my part.<br/> <b>Bottom Line</b>...I like the way you think.  <i>If I had been in that part of my brain during the entry phase, I could have seen me producing a very similar image with a very similar title.</i>  So, much of this advice would be considered "out-loud thinking" under the heading, <b>"Note to Self!"</b>  :)</td>', 'Cute!  I get the humor.  If only it was not such a serious subject in the original meaning.    When I was still a sophomoric teenager (of course, my friends would all say, "Sorry, Dude, mentally No Change today",) I tried to create my own humor by teasing that the untimely deaths of "Snap, Crackle & Pop" would be performed by a "cereal" killer.  Very Dark Humor...  :(       But as to meeting the challenge,...Dead On!   I give you a 9 for challenge parameters.  I would give you a 10, but IMHO the contrast was post-processed too thin.  Nothing more than a judgment call on my part. Bottom Line...I like the way you think.  If I had been in that part of my brain during the entry phase, I could have seen me producing a very similar image with a very similar title.  So, much of this advice would be considered "out-loud thinking" under the heading, "Note to Self!"  :)', '2006-09-03 14:21:24.000000', NULL, 1),
(2792039, 385062, 50034, '<td valign="top">For a little FUN, try a re-do in B/W...and...there you have it...a scene out of the movie version of the literary classic <u>1984</u> by George Orwell.</td>', 'For a little FUN, try a re-do in B/W...and...there you have it...a scene out of the movie version of the literary classic 1984 by George Orwell.', '2006-09-03 14:25:01.000000', NULL, 1),
(2792074, 386610, 50034, '<td valign="top">"I love texture," says my wife, "but the rich red of the bricks fights with the weathered aspect of the cement.  IMO the yellow bricks detract from the red bricks &amp; should be cropped out."  I agree &amp; I agree with her that we both love the image.<br/>   I am actually afraid to have her open her own profile on DPChallenge because though she is a hair designer by trade, she has potential to be a much better photographer than I am, even if it''s just a hobby for her.  :)</td>', '"I love texture," says my wife, "but the rich red of the bricks fights with the weathered aspect of the cement.  IMO the yellow bricks detract from the red bricks & should be cropped out."  I agree & I agree with her that we both love the image.   I am actually afraid to have her open her own profile on DPChallenge because though she is a hair designer by trade, she has potential to be a much better photographer than I am, even if it''s just a hobby for her.  :)', '2006-09-03 14:36:59.000000', NULL, 1),
